DESCRIPTION:<p>Reimagined by the visionary Tony Award&reg;-winning
  director Jamie Lloyd, Tim Rice and Andrew Lloyd Webber&rsquo;s legendary
  <em>Evita</em> returns to Broadway, starring Rachel Zegler, who won the
  Olivier Award for her acclaimed portrayal of Eva Per&oacute;n in the West
  End.&nbsp;<em><br /><br />Evita</em> features an iconic score, including
  &ldquo;Don&rsquo;t Cry For Me Argentina,&rdquo; &ldquo;Oh What a
  Circus,&rdquo; &ldquo;Another Suitcase in Another Hall,&rdquo; and the
  Oscar&reg;-winning &ldquo;You Must Love Me.&rdquo; Fueled by ambition and
  passion Eva Per&oacute;n rose from poverty to become the most powerful
  woman in Latin America. A symbol of hope for many Argentines, her star
  shone brightly as she captured the nation&rsquo;s heart and divided its
  soul.</p>
END:VEVENT
